WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.990
- Well, congrats on the Vegas show.

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:04.470
I know a lot of artists, me included,

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.900
we just love performing
and we were all just,

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.310
we had to stop for like
a year or two. Right?

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:12.134
So how is it to back to be?

00:00:12.134 --> 00:00:13.720
- I thought it would be
different, but I mean,

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.420
it was like these 18
months just disappeared

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.280
and we were back on the stage

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.850
and it looked, it felt pretty
much the same as usual.

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.180
There was one extra element
on these last couple of shows

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.550
that we did, that I'd never felt before.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.730
It felt,

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.180
yeah they were applauding.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.880
Yeah, we were all having a good time,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.890
but there was something else.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:39.540
It felt like the audience was
grateful to be in this room

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.730
and not have to worry about all the crap

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.137
that we've been dealing with.

00:00:44.137 --> 00:00:44.970
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.620
- They were laughing
and singing and happy.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.320
And I felt like everybody
was just very grateful.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.580
They were applauding me,

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.547
but they were applauding themselves.

00:00:53.547 --> 00:00:56.404
- The moment. No, we took
it for granted a little.

00:00:56.404 --> 00:00:58.930
I was just having this
conversation yesterday with someone

00:00:58.930 --> 00:00:59.830
because I literally,

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.010
I mean shows started happening

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.630
and my friends, we have been to four.

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:04.240
So we're going to one next week.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:07.530
Like, I get drunk off the energy of it.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.700
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.740
You're like, I miss it.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:10.770
I didn't know that I miss,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:14.150
I don't even really miss
performing as much as I do watching

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.330
and like being a part
of the show in that way.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:19.810
That's so amazing. And it's
awesome to listen to music,

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:20.780
but to feel it,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.613
- Yes.

00:01:21.613 --> 00:01:22.760
- and to be in a room filled
with people that you would

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.980
probably never find yourself

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.170
in the same room with in
any other circumstance

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.064
- So it's not having to
worry about everything else

00:01:28.064 --> 00:01:29.611
that we've been worrying about 18 months.

00:01:29.611 --> 00:01:30.520
- [Kelly] Escapism. Yeah.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.100
- It just disappeared for 90 minutes

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.660
and I was grateful I could
do it, but it really,

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.370
they were grateful, I was grateful.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.440
It was a great couple of nights.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.200
- Yeah. Yeah. I love that.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.281
I love seeing shows.

00:01:43.281 --> 00:01:46.880
You've also got your own musical, right?

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.070
I think that's amazing.

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:49.660
And it's got to sound incredible.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.920
You're such a great pianist
and musician and writer.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.140
- Yeah. this is the biggest

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.640
and the most important thing to me.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.430
Right now, it's a musical called "Harmony"

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.900
and it opens in New York,

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.530
down at the Yiddish Theater

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:05.960
and the little hope it goes
from there to Broadway.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.060
It's called "Harmony."

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.822
And it opens in April,

00:02:10.822 --> 00:02:14.630
this coming year and
previews start before that,

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:16.560
and you should check this one out.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.983
It's a real good one.

00:02:17.983 --> 00:02:21.040
- It takes a while for all
these projects to develop.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.730
So how long have you been working on this?

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:23.563
- [Barry] 20 years.

00:02:23.563 --> 00:02:24.660
- 20 years? Wow.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.900
- [Audience] Wow.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.860
- Yeah. Yeah, but it's worth it.

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.300
- [Kelly] Oh, my gosh.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:30.430
- You really need to check this one out.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.786
- Oh, that's amazing.

00:02:31.786 --> 00:02:32.810
So what's "Harmony?" What is it about?

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.025
Like, what's the gist.

00:02:34.025 --> 00:02:34.858
- It's about a singing group

00:02:34.858 --> 00:02:37.963
that was very, very big
in the 1920s in Germany.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:42.560
A few of them were Jews
and a few of them were not,

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:43.540
and their story.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.050
The reason we don't know who they are,

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:47.360
they were called the Comedian Harmonists,

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.190
very talented, very talented,
tremendously popular.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.260
And we don't know about them

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.080
because everything they did was destroyed.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.700
- Oh, so this is based
off of something real.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.874
I didn't get that.

00:02:57.874 --> 00:02:59.112
- A real story.

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.410
It's a real story and it's very compelling

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.000
and I'm very proud of the score.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.760
And my partner, Bruce Sussman,

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:07.600
wrote the lyrics and the book.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:11.280
And it's really deep and
funny, because they were funny,

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.910
but you really should check this one out.

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:15.370
- Wow. I can't wait to see that.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.274
That was a great sell by the way.

00:03:17.274 --> 00:03:18.107
(Barry laughing)

00:03:18.107 --> 00:03:19.187
I'm like, wow!

00:03:19.187 --> 00:03:22.759
I'm going to get you to
sell my stuff. Like, I'm in.

00:03:22.759 --> 00:03:24.020
And that's the thing too,

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.310
like, New York starting to come back.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.610
I miss shows so much.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.327
We opened this whole show
in New York this year.

00:03:28.327 --> 00:03:29.490
- [Barry] I know it's rough.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.670
- Oh, man. But it's such a city

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.350
that feels ghost-like without theater.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:37.060
- You know, Bruce told me when
we were in the middle of it,

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.060
times square was empty.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.960
All the streets that had
the theaters on it, empty.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.380
Like, you know, newspapers
just floating around

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.940
like some something out
of a science fiction.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.260
- [Kelly] Like a movie, yeah.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.400
- Yeah. It was rough.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.320
- Oh, well you have new
fans on TikTok as well,

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.350
which I love,

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.950
because this lip sync video
of "Mandy" went viral.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.110
Here it is, you've got to see it.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.791
- [Barry] Did you see it?

00:03:58.791 --> 00:04:00.700
♪ I see a memory ♪

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:02.791
♪ I never realized ♪

00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:05.148
♪ How happy you made me ♪

00:04:05.148 --> 00:04:07.271
♪ Oh, Mandy ♪

00:04:07.271 --> 00:04:12.271
♪ Well, you came and you
gave without taking ♪

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:15.151
- Oh, my God. He's adorable.

00:04:16.082 --> 00:04:18.690
So what did you think when you saw that?

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.010
- Well, I was surprised.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:24.754
I wondered how did he find
"Mandy" to lip-sync to.

00:04:24.754 --> 00:04:25.780
He's so young.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.410
- Spotify is a beautiful thing.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.640
I feel like we find things

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:30.400
like on all these streaming services now,

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.290
like even my kids are
starting to listen to music.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:33.300
They're like, "oh, I love this new song."

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.964
I'm like, "that ain't new,
that's from the '80s."

00:04:35.964 --> 00:04:37.554
- You should show them "Copacabana."

00:04:37.554 --> 00:04:38.387
They would love "Copacabana."

00:04:38.387 --> 00:04:39.930
- I know, I'm just saying
they find this music

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.575
and they think it's new. Yeah.

00:04:41.575 --> 00:04:44.160
- I wonder how he found the.

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.270
- Backstory. We need the backstory.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:49.210
Well, the video inspired
thousands of responses

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:50.043
like this one.

00:04:51.335 --> 00:04:53.244
♪ I see a memory ♪

00:04:53.244 --> 00:04:55.591
♪ I never realized ♪

00:04:55.591 --> 00:04:57.564
♪ How happy you made me ♪

00:04:57.564 --> 00:04:59.644
♪ Oh, Mandy ♪

00:04:59.644 --> 00:05:04.124
♪ Well, you came and you
gave without taking ♪

00:05:04.124 --> 00:05:06.183
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:06.183 --> 00:05:07.687
- Wait, wait, wait.

00:05:07.687 --> 00:05:08.770
And this one.

00:05:10.375 --> 00:05:12.306
♪ I see a memory ♪

00:05:12.306 --> 00:05:14.449
♪ I never realized ♪

00:05:14.449 --> 00:05:16.519
♪ How happy you made me ♪

00:05:16.519 --> 00:05:18.684
♪ Oh, Mandy ♪

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:23.666
♪ Well, you came and you
gave without taking ♪

00:05:23.666 --> 00:05:25.916
(laughing)

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.770
- So have you heard from that kid?

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:31.950
Have you heard from who
made the first video?

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:32.990
- Oh, no. No, I haven't.

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:34.810
- Oh my God. It's so great.

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:35.790
And it's so random,

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.890
which is the most amazing
part and the reactions.

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:40.040
Anyway, well we've reached out to him

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.910
and he's actually in our audience.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:44.223
So say hello to William White!

00:05:45.146 --> 00:05:47.305
(audience cheering)

00:05:47.305 --> 00:05:48.305
There he is.

00:05:49.288 --> 00:05:50.454
He's in the middle screen.

00:05:50.454 --> 00:05:51.696
- Yeah.

00:05:51.696 --> 00:05:54.168
- [Kelly] Oh, my God.
Well, meet Barry Manilow!

00:05:54.168 --> 00:05:55.802
- [Barry] Hi. Hi.

00:05:55.802 --> 00:05:57.517
- Hi, Barry.

00:05:57.517 --> 00:05:59.910
- How did you find the song?

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.040
- Yeah, it was my dad. He showed me.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.090
He's a huge fan, so he's pretty jealous

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.160
that I'm on here right now,

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.280
but his buddies love it.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:12.280
So we go for walks and he
showed me some old music

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.480
and then I found "Mandy",

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:17.060
and I was like, "oh, this is
like perfect for the ladies."

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.570
Like, it's a heartthrob music.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:19.660
I was like, all right.

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:24.660
So I went home and after
work, I was landscaping,

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:28.660
and went home and started
making "Mandy" videos.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.970
And from there it just blew up,

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:35.773
like over one weekend I hit
like 1.8 million followers.

00:06:36.624 --> 00:06:37.457
- That's amazing.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.670
- Talk about getting laid from music.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.896
- I know. I'm just
saying, that song lasts.

00:06:42.896 --> 00:06:44.314
- [Barry] You must have scored.

00:06:44.314 --> 00:06:45.914
- Some longevity with that song.

